    "created_at": "2025-07-14T18:58:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-07-14T18:58:54Z",
    "body": "Section numbers, even if they aren't stable over time, provide contextual information that's useful for understanding where you are in the document.\n\nAs someone who's using this document as a reference, it feels like there's a lack of context without section numbers. It's difficult to tell which part of the document tree I'm in - a section? a subsection? a sub subsection? And if I scroll down a page or two, am I in another section, or the same one still? \n\nIMO, ideally, there would be some way of finding out the names of all the parent sections from the section you're reading.",
